WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:09.380
Career and Technical Education is
enjoying a moment. Governors talk about it

00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:14.440
and education advocates celebrate it. Is
this a passing fad or something more?

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:19.380
Our recent analysis of media coverage finds
that CTE has been growing steadily in

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:24.390
popularity over the past two decades.
Since 1998, the number of articles

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:29.099
mentioning CTE has risen more than a
hundredfold and the number of media

00:00:29.099 --> 00:00:34.920
mentions has doubled since 2012.
Attention to CTE now dwarfs that paid to

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:39.700
education reforms like school vouchers
or personalized learning. Put in the context

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:44.160
of pop culture, press mentions of
CTE rival mentions of celebrities like

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:50.610
Kim Kardashian, Steph Curry, or Queen
Elizabeth. The rise of CTE is part of a

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:55.540
bigger trend: the increased attention to
skills training and workforce preparedness.

00:00:56.260 --> 00:01:00.520
A careful look at how CTE
got here suggests that, for better

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:06.100
or worse, it's likely to remain a focal point
of education reform in the decade to come.

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:11.180
How do you think that America's
schools can best equip students to

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:15.940
succeed after graduation? Let us know in
our poll. Also, let us know what other

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:20.280
topics you'd like our scholars to cover
in 60 seconds and be sure to LIKE and

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:25.130
subscribe for more research
and videos from AEI.

